ecause cold checker compilation regresses in the fixed matched sweep.\nKeep this pull request in draft.\nPublished head `67b21637` still contains the rejected trial and must not merge.\nLocal removal `7f9ea39b` deletes only the helper and its two call sites.\nLocal merge `c02d2b4c` preserves actual main `e4494347` and awaits retained-source validation.\n\nThe proposed final compiler and standard library sources exactly match main `e4494347`.\nThe retained changes cover receiver-query contracts and repair the kernel scheduler fixture.\nAll earlier experiment records remain intact.\nNo compiler optimization or speedup remains in the proposed final source.\n\nThe new receiver regression checks exact raw membership and method selection on x86-64, QEMU ARM64, and WASI.\nIt covers first-duplicate behavior, empty and missing names, qualified variants, direct/generic receivers, and import state.\nThe test also checks a table with 300 unions.\nThe recursive array-based membership API and the existing union index remain unchanged.\n\nThe measured trial compares main `b442b6b9` with candidate `67b21637`.\nEight fixed balanced pairs per workload and proof-cache mode produce 64 timed commands.\nSeparate cache primes and probes add eight normal commands.\nTwelve separate counter commands retain allocation and free counts.\nAll 84 commands succeed, and emitted native programs match within each workload.\nNo sample extension or favorable retry occurs.\n\nCold checker CPU medians increase from 11.8509315 to 13.118910 seconds, or 10.7%.\nSeven of eight candidate pairs are slower.\nThe other three workload and cache combinations retain lower CPU medians.\nAllocation counts and median peak RSS remain equal in all four combinations.\nThe other gains do not justify the unresolved cold checker cost.\nThe physical timing cause remains unknown.\n\nThe instruction matrix stops after this rejection.\nIts first candidate run receives SIGTERM, and all partial traces and logs remain intact.\nThere is no completed instruction comparison for this source pair.\nThe older `0e715dff` / `99fda7a6` instruction reduction remains a separate historical result for the rejected trial.\nNo external rank or normal full-run leak claim is made.\n\nThe earlier CI failure concerns `TestSelfHostKernelTwoCoreSchedulerOnQemu`.\nAll workers exit zero and frames return, but the test does not observe each worker on both cores.\nI claimed only this failure on #15118, comment 6773460833.\nThe fixture now requires each process to visit both cores before either core resumes it repeatedly.\nThe compiler, standard library, timer, worker, assertions, and budgets remain unchanged by this repair.\n\nSix ordinary main `515ddee8` repetitions pass locally, so no natural local reproduction is claimed.\nOne private slower-timer control fails the original migration and concurrency assertions.\nThe corrected fixture passes 12 standard scheduler runs, Go vet, and every original assertion under that private control.\nThis control does not establish a unique cause for the CI timing difference.\nThe `ci-full` label retains every failure in the next complete round.\n\nThe rejected source passes 147 test and subtest results across 17 suites, with zero skips.\nBoth normal compilers check their own source and retain all five E098 refusals with identical diagnostics.\nIts full normal interpreter control passes the complete Opus corpus with the expected reference TAP output.\nThese results remain source-specific.\nFresh main and retained builds, source checks, targeted tests, and full correctness controls are in progress.\nThe retained source also includes every upstream parser, mismatch-kernel, and Android repair from current main.\n\nThe validated removal will follow on this same branch with an expected-head guard.\nAll raw measurements, failures, exact source identities, and the rejection decision will follow in a separate evidence archive.\nKeep this PR in draft until the retained source passes complete exact-head relevant CI.\n\nPart of #11534.\n","labels":[{"id":12097060284,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSVpu_M8AAAAC0Qp9vA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JakeChampion/lang/labels/ci-full","name":"ci-full","description":"Do not cancel sibling CI lanes when one fails on this PR","color":"5319E7","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-10T16:17:50Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:55:03Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"837d756a320425ef90f9886ce64b55bffa110558","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"JakeChampion:perf/index-receiver-union-membership","ref":"perf/index-receiver-union-membership","repo":{"id":1230663420,"node_id":"R_kgDOSVpu_A","name":"lang","full_name":"JakeChampion/lang","owner":{"login":"JakeChampion","id":1569131,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NjkxMzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1569131?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JakeChampion","html_url":"https://github.com/JakeChampion","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JakeChampion/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JakeChampion/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JakeChampion/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JakeChampion/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JakeChampion/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JakeChampion/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JakeChampion/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JakeChampion/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JakeChampion/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":null,"homepage":null,"language":"Rust","visibility":"public","is_template":false,"topics":[